Changes in superServe: typed messages and original-text references, a strict
serialized UTF-8 byte budget including JSON escaping and metadata, Unicode-safe
head/tail clipping, and an on-demand projection of persisted HMM business state.
The adaptation also customizes the native DSH summarizer with numbered
checkpoints, recent original messages, bounded model output and cancellation.
Successive checkpoints inherit bounded original-message indexes while preserving
clipping metadata and explicitly reporting inherited omission lower bounds.
Original append-only Session records are retained and read through a
controller-scoped history tool. DS Bot's runtime is not a dependency.
